# HTTP Error Code Cheat Sheet

| Status | Meaning | What to check |
|---|---|---|
| 200 | OK | Request succeeded |
| 201 | Created | Record saved successfully |
| 400 | Bad Request | Form data |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Login session |
| 403 | Forbidden | User permissions |
| 404 | Not Found | API URL / PHP file |
| 405 | Method Not Allowed | GET versus POST |
| 409 | Conflict | Existing reservation |
| 500 | Internal Server Error | PHP / database / application error |
| 502 | Bad Gateway | PHP backend / Vite proxy connection |

## Golden Rule

**Check the browser's Network tab before changing code.**

If login or submission suddenly stops working:

1. Check whether MySQL is running.
2. Check whether PHP is reachable.
3. Check the failed request's HTTP status.
4. Read the response message.
5. Fix the actual cause rather than randomly modifying working code.

